meta {
  name: Confirm Holiday Proposal (None, 404)
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hr/calendar/proposals/2099/confirm
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{hrAdminAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "dates": []
  }
}

tests {
  test("a year with no proposal is a 404", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(404);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /hr/calendar/proposals/:year/confirm · …/dismiss (PAC-161)

  - **Module:** `hr` · **Permission:** `agency:hr:admin`

  The Q4 worker job (`propose-next-year-holidays`, daily) writes a
  **proposal** of next year's holidays onto the calendar once it is October on
  the agency's clock — one per agency per year, never auto-inserted — and
  notifies the `agency:hr:admin` holders (`hr.holidays_proposed`). The
  settings page shows it as a banner; `GET /hr/calendar` carries it as
  `pendingProposal`.

  - **confirm** — body `{ "dates": ["YYYY-MM-DD", …] }`, a subset of the
    proposal's items (may be empty). Writes the chosen dates as `holiday`
    rows with `source: "proposal"`, skipping any date already on the calendar,
    and marks the proposal `confirmed`. A date not in the proposal is a `400`.
  - **dismiss** — no body; marks it `dismissed`.

  Both are idempotent on a decided proposal (`200`, no change). This request
  exercises the `404` for a year nobody proposed; a live proposal only exists
  after the job has run.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  { "year": 2027, "status": "confirmed", "proposedAt": "…", "items": [{ "date": "2027-01-01", "name": "New Year's Day", "type": "public", "substitute": false }] }
  ```
}
